---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Clear explanation of what data Retenqo's website, hosting provider, GitHub Releases, and Android app process."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <p
      class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-[var(--accent-primary)] uppercase"
    >
      Privacy
    </p>
    <h1
      class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--text-primary)] sm:text-4xl"
    >
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-base text-[var(--text-secondary)]">
      Retenqo is built on a simple principle: your personal memories belong on
      your device. This policy explains what happens across the website,
      hosting, APK distribution, and Android app.
    </p>

    <div
      class="mt-10 space-y-8 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--text-secondary)]"
    >
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          1. This Website
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          This static website does not use tracking cookies, third-party
          advertising, user fingerprinting, or analytics scripts. We do not
          collect personal information or run user accounts.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          2. Hosting &amp; Network Requests
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The website is served as static files over HTTPS via Cloudflare Pages.
          Like any web host, Cloudflare may process standard HTTP request
          metadata (such as IP address and user agent) for security, DDoS
          protection, and routing.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          3. APK Downloads via GitHub Releases
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          When you click to download the Android APK, your browser connects
          directly to GitHub Releases. GitHub's own privacy policy applies to
          that download request.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)]">
          4. The Retenqo Android Application
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Memories, commitments, and embeddings are stored locally on your
          device. Core AI inference runs on-device. Network access is only used
          when you explicitly choose to download an on-device model or check for
          updates.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
